<newsitem itemid="228012" id="root" date="1996-12-02" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Rembrandt lifts interim shr, div.</title>
<headline>Rembrandt lifts interim shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Sept 30, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr:</p>
<p>    - pre-excepts (cts)    174.7	 vs 128.0</p>
<p>    - post-excepts (cts)   192.9	 vs 128.9</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		   29.4	 vs  24.5</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   1,007	  vs 673</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		     243	  vs 693</p>
<p>    Tax			    73	  vs 249</p>
<p>    Interest paid		55	  vs  68</p>
<p>    Dividend income	   230	  vs 113</p>
<p>    Turnover		  2,934	  vs 4,597</p>
<p>    Share of associates'    550	   vs 149</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	 125	   vs   2</p>
<p>Full name: Rembrandt Group Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said the results were not directly comparable because of the exchange of former wholly-owned tobacco interests for an investment in Rothmans International Holdings in October 1995 and the disposal of Hunt Lechaurs &amp; Hepburn's hardwood timnber interests in April 1996.</p>
<p>The dividend was declared in August and paid in October.  </p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters expected earnings per share before exceptional items to climb to between 160 and 162.6 cents with consensus at 161 cents.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town Newsroom + 27 21 252238</p>
</text>
